<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, minimum-scale=0.5, maximum-scale=5">

    <!-- Theme Mode-->
    <script>
        const isAutoTheme = {% if site.color_theme == 'auto' %}true{% else %}false{% endif %};
        const preferredTheme = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
        if (isAutoTheme) {
            document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', sessionStorage.getItem('theme') ?? preferredTheme);
        } else {
            document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', "{{ site.color_theme | default: 'light' }}");
        }
    </script>

    <!-- CSS -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/main.css' | relative_url }}">

    <!--Favicon-->
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{ '/assets/images/favicon.svg' | relative_url }}">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="{{ '/assets/images/favicon-32.png' | relative_url }}">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ '/assets/images/apple-touch-icon.png' | relative_url }}">

    <!-- seo tags -->
    <meta property="og:image" content="{{ page.thumbnail | default: page['feature-img'] | default: site.header_feature_image | absolute_url }}">
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
    <meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png">
    {%- assign _alt_t = page.title | default: site.title -%}
    {%- capture _alt_d %}{% include defang-text.html text=_alt_t %}{% endcapture -%}
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ _alt_d }}">
    {%- comment -%} jekyll-seo-tag emits `twitter:card=summary` for any page without an SEO
    `image:` key, and this site wires cards through `thumbnail:` instead, so left alone X saw two
    card tags on every page. The plugin's output is captured and that one tag removed; the
    `summary_large_image` tag below is then the only card declaration. The replace is an exact
    string match on what jekyll-seo-tag 2.8 (the GitHub Pages pin) writes, so if a future plugin
    version changes its markup the replace is a no-op and the page simply reverts to the old
    duplicate rather than losing anything. The plugin's own `twitter:title` is kept and the
    hand-written one dropped, so title is emitted once too. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture _seo %}{% seo %}{% endcapture -%}
    {%- assign _seo = _seo | replace: '<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />', '' -%}
    {%- comment -%} The display strings of the SEO tag (tab title, og:title, twitter:title, the descriptions, the JSON-LD headline and description) are defanged; its URLs stay exact (defang-head.html). {%- endcomment %}
    {% include defang-head.html text=_seo %}
    {%- capture _sd %}{% if page.layout == "post" %}{% if page.url contains "/reports/" or page.url contains "/hunting-detections/" %}{% include structured-data.liquid %}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if page.layout == "ioc-table" or page.url == "/ioc-feeds/" or page.url == "/stix/" or page.url == "/feeds/misp/" or page.url == "/hunting-detections/" %}{% include structured-data-dataset.liquid %}{% endif %}{% endcapture %}
    {% include defang-head.html text=_sd %}

    <!-- RSS -->
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/atom+xml" title="{{ site.title | default: 'Title' }}" href="{{ 'feed.xml' | absolute_url }}"/>
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/feed+json" title="{{ site.title | default: 'Title' }}" href="{{ 'feed.json' | absolute_url }}"/>
    {%- if page.url == '/wire/' %}
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/atom+xml" title="{{ site.title | default: 'Title' }}: The Wire" href="{{ 'wire/feed.xml' | absolute_url }}"/>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if page.url == '/changes/' %}
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/atom+xml" title="{{ site.title | default: 'Title' }}: Report Changes" href="{{ 'changes/feed.xml' | absolute_url }}"/>
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/feed+json" title="{{ site.title | default: 'Title' }}: Report Changes" href="{{ 'changes/feed.json' | absolute_url }}"/>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if page.url contains '/hunting-detections/' %}
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/atom+xml" title="{{ site.title | default: 'Title' }}: Detection Rules" href="{{ 'hunting-detections/feed.xml' | absolute_url }}"/>
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/feed+json" title="{{ site.title | default: 'Title' }}: Detection Rules" href="{{ 'hunting-detections/feed.json' | absolute_url }}"/>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- comment -%} jekyll-feed's {% feed_meta %} used to follow here and wrote the site feed
    link a second time (the hand-written one above is the one with the title and the
    siblings). Removed 2026-10-10; the plugin still does nothing else here because the
    hand-written feed.xml takes precedence over the one it would generate. {%- endcomment -%}

    {%- comment -%} Twitter/X card. `twitter:title` comes from jekyll-seo-tag above; the
    `summary` card it also writes is stripped there, so these are the only card, description
    and image tags on the page. og:image (used by Slack/Discord/LinkedIn/etc.) is set above
    and is correct everywhere. {%- endcomment -%}
    <!-- Twitter Cards -->
    {%- assign _tw_d0 = page.description | default: site.description | strip_html | strip_newlines | truncate: 200 -%}
    {%- capture _tw_d %}{% include defang-text.html text=_tw_d0 %}{% endcapture -%}
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ _tw_d }}">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ page.thumbnail | default: page['feature-img'] | default: site.header_feature_image | absolute_url }}">
    <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="{{ _alt_d }}">
    <!-- Local override: project design system -->
    {%- comment -%} Versioned per build so markup and stylesheet always ship as a pair.
    GitHub Pages caches assets for ten minutes; without this, a returning reader got new
    HTML styled by the previous CSS for that window (seen 2026-10-09 on the nav drawer,
    which rendered as an unstyled list). build_revision is the commit the build ran from,
    so the URL only changes when main changes; a local build falls back to the build time. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture _css_v -%}{% if site.github.build_revision %}{{ site.github.build_revision | slice: 0, 10 }}{% else %}{{ site.time | date: '%s' }}{% endif %}{%- endcapture -%}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/custom.css' | relative_url }}?v={{ _css_v }}-text-accents-1">
    {%- comment -%} Report tabs stylesheet (A23). It used to be linked from inside <body> by
    post.html, after the header had begun painting. The layout's rendered output is the `content`
    string here, so the tabbed-report test is the same marker that layout emits. Order stays after
    custom.css, which is where the body link effectively sat. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if content contains 'hl-page hl-report-page' %}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/hl-report-tabs.css' | relative_url }}?v=20261112.1" data-rv-chrome data-pagefind-ignore>
    {%- endif %}
    <link rel="preload" href="{{ '/assets/fonts/space-grotesk.woff2' | relative_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preload" href="{{ '/assets/fonts/source-serif-4-var.woff2' | relative_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preload" href="{{ '/assets/fonts/ibm-plex-sans-var.woff2' | relative_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>

    {%- comment -%} Cloudflare Web Analytics, JS-snippet install. This site is deliberately
    DNS-only (grey cloud) so that requests go browser -> GitHub Pages and never traverse
    Cloudflare. That means Cloudflare's "Automatic setup" option, which injects this beacon
    at the edge, can never fire here and will report zero forever. The snippet install is the
    correct mechanism for an unproxied origin. No cookies, no client-side state, so no consent
    banner is required. {%- endcomment -%}
    {% if site.cloudflare_analytics_token and site.cloudflare_analytics_token != "" %}
    <script type="module" src="https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js" data-cf-beacon='{"token": "{{ site.cloudflare_analytics_token }}"}'></script>
    {% endif %}
</head>
